    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "honestly the hotlines just feel like someone reading a script. they don't get it. they don't understand that my life is actually over. there is no \"getting through this\" when everything that made me *me* is gone. when you've been cast out like this, it's like you're just a shell. it feels more like a mercy to just stop fighting the fact that i've already been erased.",
